// Markup: what prose means, wherever it's written. The grammar says how it's
// read; this folder says what each form builds, what renders and what the
// prose view projects.
include = [
  "./writing.heron.md",
  "./text.heron.md",
  "./links.heron",
  "./inserts.heron.md",
  "./tags.heron",
  "./components.heron.md",
  "./from_markdown.heron",
  "./long_form.heron",
  "./authored_pages.heron",
  "./lens_marks.heron.md",
  "./prose_view.heron.md",
]

@lens(user, developer)
| Markup is the prose [layer](#heron.language.specifications.layers.layer) of the format: Markdown's inline text with links to nodes, `$` inserts and [component tags](#language.markup.tags.component_tag), the `std/doc` components it places, and the projection text linters read. The [grammar](#language.grammar.prose) says how each form is read; this section says what it means.

prose_stays_true: goal(measure = "Prose links and inserts never point at nothing.") {{
  Authors write prose that links to and quotes the tree, so it changes when the tree changes.
}}
